# FleetLink UI Standards

## Design System Location

```
mobile/src/shared/
├── components/
│   ├── Button/
│   ├── Input/
│   ├── Card/
│   ├── Modal/
│   └── loading/
│       ├── Skeleton.tsx
│       ├── Shimmer.tsx
│       ├── EmptyState.tsx
│       └── ErrorState.tsx
└── theme/
    ├── colors.ts
    ├── spacing.ts
    ├── typography.ts
    ├── radius.ts
    └── index.ts
```

All UI must use these shared primitives. Do not create one-off buttons or inputs in feature folders.

## Required Reusable Components

### Button

```tsx
<Button
  title="Accept Trip"
  onPress={handleAccept}
  variant="primary"       // primary | secondary | outline | danger | ghost
  size="md"               // sm | md | lg
  loading={isPending}
  disabled={!canAccept}
/>
```

- Handles loading spinner inside button
- Disabled state styled consistently
- Min touch target 44x44

### Input

```tsx
<Input
  label="Email"
  value={value}
  onChangeText={onChange}
  error={errors.email?.message}
  keyboardType="email-address"
  autoCapitalize="none"
/>
```

- Integrates with React Hook Form via `Controller`
- Error text below field
- Label always visible (no placeholder-only labels)

### Card

```tsx
<Card padding="md" onPress={onPress}>
  <Text style={styles.title}>{trip.pickup}</Text>
</Card>
```

- Consistent shadow, radius, background from theme
- Optional `onPress` for tappable cards

### Modal

```tsx
<Modal
  visible={isOpen}
  onClose={onClose}
  title="Confirm Action"
>
  <Text>Are you sure?</Text>
  <Button title="Confirm" onPress={onConfirm} />
</Modal>
```

- Backdrop dismiss, consistent animation
- Title + close button in header

## Theme Tokens Only

```typescript
// spacing.ts
export const spacing = {
  xs: 4,
  sm: 8,
  md: 16,
  lg: 24,
  xl: 32,
  xxl: 48,
} as const;

// colors.ts — light and dark
export const lightColors = {
  primary: '#2563EB',
  background: '#F8FAFC',
  surface: '#FFFFFF',
  textPrimary: '#0F172A',
  textSecondary: '#64748B',
  error: '#DC2626',
  success: '#16A34A',
  border: '#E2E8F0',
};

export const darkColors = {
  primary: '#3B82F6',
  background: '#0F172A',
  surface: '#1E293B',
  textPrimary: '#F8FAFC',
  textSecondary: '#94A3B8',
  error: '#EF4444',
  success: '#22C55E',
  border: '#334155',
};
```

**Never use raw hex values in components.** Import from theme.

## Spacing System

| Token | Value | Use |
|-------|-------|-----|
| `xs` | 4 | Icon gaps, tight padding |
| `sm` | 8 | Between related elements |
| `md` | 16 | Card padding, section gaps |
| `lg` | 24 | Screen padding, section margins |
| `xl` | 32 | Large section breaks |
| `xxl` | 48 | Hero spacing |

Screen horizontal padding: `spacing.lg` (24px) standard.

## Typography

| Token | Size | Weight | Use |
|-------|------|--------|-----|
| `heading1` | 28 | 700 | Screen titles |
| `heading2` | 22 | 600 | Section titles |
| `heading3` | 18 | 600 | Card titles |
| `body` | 16 | 400 | Primary text |
| `bodySmall` | 14 | 400 | Secondary text |
| `caption` | 12 | 400 | Labels, metadata |
| `label` | 14 | 500 | Form labels, buttons |

## Component Creation Rules

Before creating a new UI component, check:

1. Does `Button`, `Input`, `Card`, or `Modal` cover this with props/variants?
2. Is this used in 2+ places? → `shared/components/`
3. Is this domain-specific? → `features/{name}/components/` but still use theme tokens

## Dark Mode

- Every component must work in light and dark mode
- Use `useTheme().colors` — never hardcode
- Test both modes before considering UI complete
- Elevation/shadows may differ between modes

## Consistency Checklist

- [ ] Uses shared Button/Input/Card/Modal
- [ ] Colors from theme tokens
- [ ] Spacing from spacing tokens
- [ ] Typography from typography tokens
- [ ] Works in light and dark mode
- [ ] Loading/empty/error states use shared components
- [ ] Touch targets ≥ 44x44

## Anti-Patterns

| Pattern | Fix |
|---------|-----|
| Custom button in feature folder | Extend shared `Button` variant |
| `marginTop: 13` | `spacing.md` or `spacing.sm` |
| `fontSize: 17` | `typography.body` |
| Different card styles per screen | Shared `Card` component |
| Hardcoded white background | `colors.surface` |
